description:
WHY: the M0 done-when in one command; this fixture is the spine every later milestone extends. A running 40-bit slice reveals more than more architecture.

WHAT (`src/cairn/cli.py`, `src/cairn/m0.py`, `tests/e2e/test_m0_slice.py`)
`uv run cairn m0-run --bits 40 --seed 1 --db var/substrate.sqlite --bundle deploy/gate-bundle.sqlite --pin deploy/gate-bundle.pin --log DEBUG`:
1. open the bundle against the pin (fail closed on mismatch); run the gate plan self-tests (bead m0-gate-plan-selftests = cairn-m0-e0s.11) — any failure aborts before step 2;
2. require `certified(toy_curve identity)` (bead m0-skill-selftest-cert = cairn-m0-e0s.7; predicate in cairn-m0-e0s.4) else refuse `uncertified-revision`;
3. tier gate admits the Tier-0 launch (bead m0-gate-bundle-pin-tier-gate = cairn-m0-e0s.10) → gate_runs row; the launch names the slice's own hypothesis object, written here if absent (cairn-m0-e0s.5; a same-hash insert is a no-op): `{target_family:'toy_curve', claimed:{model:'c_ln_p_tries'}, method_identity:{interface_version:'toy_curve/1', params:{}}, declared_parameter_ranges:{bits:[bits,bits]}, sampling_distribution:null}` — a Tier-0 launch needs no ticket, so the object only supplies the key the gate run records; the launch carries the toy_curve `CostProfile.evaluate(bits)` (production and verification core-s, judged against the boundary table and a remaining budget of 3600 core-s, a constant of `m0.py` until the grant mechanics of M3) and the toy_curve `skill_identity_hash` (cairn-m0-e0s.6), whose `certified()`/`yanked()` standing the gate resolves;
4. runner launches `toy_curve(40, seed)` (bead m0-skill-runner-receipt = cairn-m0-e0s.9) → node A: generator output (manifest hash, receipt, cost tag tier0, certificate ref);
5. derivation fixture, deterministic (seeded from H(node A hash ‖ 'derive')): draw `x ∈ [1,n-1]`, `Q = xP` via cypari2; write node B: derivation receipt `{instance_hash, x_commit=H(x), Q}`; write a synthetic claim statement node (cairn-m0-e0s.5) whose `quantities` carry the instance `(p,a,b,n,P,Q)` so the verifier's instance is gate-read from a statement node (PLAN §4), `instance_hash` under `cairn/instance/v1` (cairn-m0-e0s.3);
6. verifier (bead m0-tier0-verifier = cairn-m0-e0s.8) on the statement node's instance with the fixture's x → node C: verifier result (accepted, reason, digests, rc) bound to instance_hash;
7. node D: gate-run record for the verifier run (bundle hash, pin hash, plan step, instance hash, result);
8. negative arm (expected FAIL, recorded): one-coordinate and one-scalar negatives → two `verifier_result` nodes with accepted=false and their `gate_runs` rows with result='fail' (a verifier run is a gate run, not a skill attempt — cairn-m0-e0s.8: it writes no `attempts` row and is never served from any cache); and a `Submission` naming its own `(P, Q)` (a different on-curve pair with a matching x) → refused before any subprocess spawns, recorded as a `gate_runs` row (gate='verifier', result='refused', reasons=['submitter-named-instance']) with no `verifier_result` node — the done-when's fourth verifier clause, recorded in the slice;
9. summary table (node kind, hash, replay grade, cost tag, self-test ref); exit 0 iff A–D exist, C.accepted, both negatives FAIL and the submitter-named submission is refused. Exit dictionary (cairn-m0-e0s.17; registered `read_only=False, json=True, aliases=('run',)` — the alias spelling .17's table names, so `cairn run --bits 40 --seed 1` resolves): 2 GATE_REFUSED for the three aborts — pin mismatch (`next_command` = the re-pin sequence of cairn-m0-e0s.10), a failing gate plan (`cairn gate selftest --json`), `uncertified-revision` (`cairn selftest toy-curve --db D --bundle X --pin Y`) — and when the attempt closes DISAGREE or BUDGET_EXCEEDED or step 6's verifier does not accept; 4 BACKEND when the attempt closes FAIL (the skill subprocess died or wrote malformed output); 3 ENVIRONMENT when gp or a deploy file is missing; `--json` prints the summary as one document `{schema_version, nodes: [{kind, hash, replay_grade, cost_tag, selftest_ref}], negatives, refused_submission, exit_code}`.
Logging: each step logs (step, input hashes, gate_runs row id, verdict, timings) through `cairn.log`; `--log DEBUG` adds gp argv and stdin/stdout/stderr digests and the subprocess argv of the skill launch; the e2e test captures stderr and asserts one record per step 1–8 and the verifier verdict records for the negatives.
E2E TEST (`tests/e2e/test_m0_slice.py`): in a tmp dir runs the full operator sequence through the CLI — `cairn bundle build --src bundle/ --bundle <tmp>/gate-bundle.sqlite` → `cairn bundle pin --bundle <tmp>/gate-bundle.sqlite --pin <tmp>/gate-bundle.pin` → `cairn attest init --attest <tmp>/attestations.log --bundle <tmp>/gate-bundle.sqlite --pin <tmp>/gate-bundle.pin` (it reads `W` from the pinned bundle, cairn-m0-e0s.10) → `cairn selftest toy-curve --db <tmp>/substrate.sqlite --bundle <tmp>/gate-bundle.sqlite --pin <tmp>/gate-bundle.pin` (certifies the revision under the pinned bundle's verifier config, cairn-m0-e0s.7; without it step 2 refuses) → `cairn m0-run ... --db <tmp>/substrate.sqlite --bundle <tmp>/gate-bundle.sqlite --pin <tmp>/gate-bundle.pin --attest <tmp>/attestations.log` (every path through the global options of cairn-m0-e0s.1, accepted before or after the subcommand; no subcommand-specific path flag); asserts A–D, the two negative nodes and the refused-submission `gate_runs` row (no `verifier_result` node, no gp stdout digest); same seed re-run ⇒ same node-A hash (Replayable) and the second run is served from cache (no new attempt) while `--skip-cache-lookup` records a fresh attempt with the same manifest; different seed ⇒ different; corrupt the pin (after `chflags nouappnd`, since a flagged file refuses overwrite, rename and unlink) ⇒ exit ≠ 0 before any skill launch (no attempt row); teardown un-flags every `uappnd` file the test created under the tmp dir (pytest cannot remove a flagged file); uncertified skill (a fresh `--db` on which `cairn selftest` never ran — a `skill_certificates` row cannot be deleted, cairn-m0-e0s.4's append-only trigger refuses it) ⇒ refused; the log assertions above. Document the fresh-clone run (`git clone` → `uv sync` → `uv run pytest` → `uv run cairn bundle build --src bundle/` → `uv run cairn bundle pin` → `uv run cairn attest init` → `uv run cairn selftest toy-curve` → `uv run cairn m0-run --bits 40 --seed 1`) in the close comment.

TEST PLAN (shapes)
- Scrubbed golden: `tests/goldens/m0_run_transcript.golden` = the ordered step log of `cairn m0-run --bits 40 --seed 1` (one line per step 1–9 and per negative: step name, verdict, reason codes, node kind) with every hash scrubbed to `[HASH]`, every `wall_ms` to `[MS]`, every path to `[PATH]` and the bundle/pin hashes to `[BUNDLE]`/`[PIN]` by a `scrub()` in `tests/conftest.py`; exact after scrubbing; volatility 2 (deterministic in shape; moves only when a step is added or a verdict vocabulary changes); regenerated only with `UPDATE_GOLDENS=1 uv run pytest tests/e2e/test_m0_slice.py -k transcript` and an attributed commit; the e2e test asserts it beside the existing per-step `json_test_log` record checks (one record per step 1–8, in order, each with `gate_runs` row id where one exists).
- Mock-free enforcement: `tests/unit/test_no_mocks_in_integration.py` (epic rule) covers `tests/e2e/`; the slice's negatives and the submitter-named refusal are real verifier runs and a real pre-spawn refusal — the only seam touched is none.
- Failure-path convergence: the three abort paths (pin mismatch; uncertified skill; a gate-plan self-test failure — the test writes an empty file at `--attest` instead of running `cairn attest init`, so the `waiver_cannot_advance` step finds no fixture waiver at record 0 (cairn-m0-e0s.11), the plan fails and the command aborts before step 2 with no attempt row) are one `@pytest.mark.parametrize` over `(setup_delta, expected_exit, expected_log_reason)` — `expected_exit` is 2 for all three — where each runs the real CLI under tmp_path; the per-step log-record assertion (a missing step record fails the test) is a separate assertion on the green run, not a setup delta; `db_snapshot` after the green run records `attempts` and `gate_runs` counts (one attempt, the expected gate runs) and the test counts `nodes` by kind — the four slice nodes A–D plus the two negative `verifier_result` nodes, three `verifier_result` rows with exactly one accepted — so a duplicated node shows in the log.
- Layer: e2e through the real console script only; no unit tests here (nothing pure lives in `m0.py` that is not already covered by its owning bead).

SCOPE (PLAN §13 M1): Prover + independent Skeptic + ladder, with the ladder's baseline skills — `rho_dp` (rho with distinguished points and the §3 witness certificate), `bsgs` (the refutation floor) and the gate-owned instance-maker — each shipping the §2 self-test. Decompose this epic into granular beads when M0 closes (the child beads below are component-grain placeholders labeled needs-decomposition; do not pre-decompose the research tree, CLAUDE.md).

OPERATOR DECISIONS THAT BIND M1 (confirmed; PLAN §16): (1) gmpy2 Hasse-interval BSGS enters as the implementation axis; (2) compiled rho/BSGS baseline funded only if the interpreted 60-bit rung (bead m0-rho60-measure) cannot finish inside the Tier-1 budget; (3) Tier-2 spend requires an open operator session until M3; (4) Reframer drafts claim statements, human ratifies through the human path; (5) yanks and `salt` are human-only; (6) a Linux container enters at M1 with the formalization gate (PROVEN gold tier needs Linux `landrun`; macOS fake-landrun dev-only); (10) Tier-1 cumulative edge = 4× the measured ladder per-run cost (CONJECTURE), set here; (12) fastest arithmetic implementation for the clock-tolerance check measured here (gmpy2 vs cypari2 vs a C reference) and recorded in the gate bundle.

DONE WHEN: every fixture in the M1 planted corpus is caught under a cold cache (`skip_cache_lookup`), INCONCLUSIVE counting as an escape, and no matched true advance is rejected; minimum corpus ≥ 30 plantings across:
(a) a BSGS-beating claim whose ops at 50 bits are ≥ generic rho and whose pre-registered model claims a sub-rho cost → the in-sample model-miss REJECT (a claim honest about a ≥ rho cost sits inside the band; INCONCLUSIVE is its correct verdict, as for control (k));
(b) a correct-ops claim that fails `xP == Q` on a fresh ladder instance → REJECT, yank the revision, write an `implementation` ledger entry against it and no `measured` entry on the hypothesis key;
(c) a Lean Solution with `sorryAx` or an extra axiom;
(d) a Lean Solution proving a strictly weaker statement than the Challenge;
(e) a small-numbers pattern that dies under the counterexample hunt;
(f) a claim seeking STRONG-EMPIRICAL with no repro node;
(g) statistical evidence offered for PROVEN;
(h) a PROVEN claim with a weaker premise in its transitive closure;
(i) a non-reproducible measurement;
and ≥ 4 positive controls that must PASS (the must-PASS half of §4's gate discipline):
(j) rho with the negation map, pre-registered at ≈ 0.886√n and submitted against the plain-rho baseline, is KEPT (its √2 on group operations at equal memory is a known answer; the ladder plan's trial count is the smallest that KEEPs it with margin);
(k) the A/A null arm submitted as a claim returns INCONCLUSIVE, never KEEP or REJECT;
(l) a Lean Solution matching its Challenge exactly with axioms inside the allow-list, with an `approve` `review_verdict` recorded against the claim statement hash through the human path, reaches PROVEN; the same artifact without the verdict, or with one naming a superseded statement hash, stays below it;
(m) a reproducible Tier-1 measurement of a computed fact (a curve order) with its repro node is admitted by `justify` to STRONG-EMPIRICAL, while a `statistical` or `repro_node` offered for a statement carrying a cost model returns the CONJECTURE ceiling; the same computed fact from a revision whose every corpus origin is `author_supplied` with no postcondition arm and no covering cross-check returns that ceiling; a `Verifiable` node whose only verifier ships in its producer's revision is graded `AuditOnly` and returns that ceiling.
Tier-gate fixtures: a synthetic KEEP_IN_SAMPLE table admits the 60-bit rung of its own hypothesis key and is refused for every other Tier-2 launch; a KEEP table is refused for a launch whose hypothesis key, method identity or implementation revision differs from the table's; a launch of a yanked or uncertified revision is refused whatever ticket it holds; a launch declaring Tier 1 for a production cost the boundary table assigns Tier 2 is refused; a claim carrying both a cost model and a correctness conjecture is refused Tier 2 while either its KEEP table or its SURVIVED record is absent; a Tier-3 request holding KEEP and no Tier-2 node is refused; a branch on the Tier-1 ticket whose worker launches would carry its hypothesis key's charge past the Tier-1 cumulative edge is refused at the crossing launch while a second ladder run on the same key is admitted; a claim whose hypothesis object names the target family with a cost model below the generic bound is routed to the router's top class and holds no Tier-3 ticket without the §10 sign-off.
Escrow and yank fixtures: a launch whose verification component the remaining budget cannot cover is refused; a reservation is spent by the §3 policy's first check and released unspent on status ≠ OK or disown; a Tier-2/3-grade node with a deferred check keeps its reservation after its attempt and branch reach a terminal status; a yank disowns every attempt inside its reach — served from no cache, no ticket, absent to `justify` — while attempts outside it stand.
Ladder-execution fixtures: a dispatch whose method identity differs from its hypothesis object's is refused before any trial; a planted method whose self-reported count is below the gate's count by more than the tolerance is REJECTed; a planted method doing its own coordinate arithmetic with dummy counted calls does not reach KEEP; a planted method opening a network socket or writing outside the scratch path fails the ladder's self-test; a planted method holding a BSGS-sized table in process memory while reporting zero table bytes exceeds the 50-bit cap on the gate's own measurement.
Dispatch canary: a distinct token planted in each settings source (project- and user-level instruction files, a skill file, the working tree's status) is absent from the request bytes the dispatch path emits where observable and from a dispatched worker's echoed context otherwise; the grounding record names which form ran; a gate self-test of the dispatch path re-run on every toolchain or SDK change whose failure yanks the path.

ADDS (PLAN §13 M1 list; each lands in a child bead): the ladder protocol (§6) with pre-registered model and frozen method identity, commit-ordered instance entropy, gate-owned operation counter, comparison protocol and trial-count sizing, typed verdicts with the ledger kind each REJECT predicate writes (the REFUTED/PARKED entry record lands here, written by the ladder's REJECT and the hunt's KILLED; the preflight that reads it arrives at M2), the in-sample check, the memory cap at the floor rungs and the memory-model check with the gate's RSS-and-scratch measurement, the compiled counted object with its recorded rate ratio and the clock and wall-clock checks, the ladder-tested method's allow-list (no undeclared arithmetic backend, no network, no writable path but the scratch path), patience ceiling, A/A null arm and out-of-sample rung, the per-rung reference rate of the clock check, per-trial replay grades and the table's reproducibility record, the budget ceiling and the verification escrow's reservation, spend and release with yank reach and `disowned` propagation, the counterexample-hunt record (§7), the human queue as a typed object with its closing rule and the `acknowledgment` record (§10, §4), the `review_verdict` node and its place in the PROVEN derivation (§7), the formalization gate's challenge/solution protocol (§7) with its gate-compiled Challenge, gate-owned axiom computation, claim-statement-to-formal-statement binding and planted-`sorry` and wrong-statement fixtures — M1 builds and probes the statement hasher and measures the gate's cost on a mathlib-importing Challenge before the fixture corpus is sized — the statement pre-filters, the reproducibility gate's re-run policy (§3) with the `Verifiable` owner rule, the transitive `justified_by` query of §7 that fixture (h) exercises, the cost-model scoping of `justify`'s kind map and its producer-standing ceiling (§7, §2), the cumulative edge of §5, the §7 disagreement protocol, the proportional-scrutiny router and the no-go checklist's presence check (§8) with the router as its consumer and the `nogo_review` node the tier gate reads, and the M1 decision on the small-numbers floor (§15 P1).

§15 P4 (decide-by M1–M2; its inputs are M1's and the keep-or-drop decision is recorded by the M2 epic cairn-m2-vgh): the operational alarms — a split-conformal anomaly flag on ladder and self-test measurements (order-statistic threshold returning +∞ when the sample is too small, never clamping), a one-sided bounded-mean e-process on `log(measured/declared cost)` read from the execution receipt's measured-versus-declared ratio, and repeated `TierRefused` records on one hypothesis key as a third input — are strategy-layer drift monitors, never enforcement: a fired alarm is a human-queue item of class `cost_drift` and a strategy input the orchestrator's tick may read to park with `budget_preempt`; it moves no tag, ticket or scrutiny class. Their inputs exist from M1 (the ladder's tables, the self-test records, the receipts, `tier_refusals`); the keep-or-drop decision (one that never fires on anything the ladder or the ceiling misses is dropped) is recorded by M2 close (cairn-m2-vgh).

STACK FACTS TO GROUND AT M1 (CONJECTURE until probed): Lean toolchain install (pin `leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc1`, elan absent on this Mac); `leanchecker --fresh` cost on a mathlib-importing Challenge (32.3 s measured mathlib-free); comparator gold tier needs Linux `landrun`; the statement hasher over `ConstantInfo` closure is inferred from the comparator's `compareAt` and must be built and probed; `chattr +a` semantics in the container.
